  "description" : "Re-cast an irregular acquisition series onto a regular calendar (e.g. every 16 days, or monthly) so downstream series models see a uniform grid. Methods: nearest (closest observation within max_window_days, ties -> earlier), window_mean (mean of the observations inside the window), linear (time-weighted interpolation between the bracketing observations), whittaker (penalized smoother defined on the calendar grid; bridges data-free runs up to max_gap_nodes). No method extrapolates past the observed span. Every calendar point carries valid_count / filled_count provenance bands so synthetic values stay distinguishable from observed ones.",
  "display_name" : "Temporal Regularize (Regular Calendar)",
